+`~/.pi/skills/` is the only source. `~/.pi/scripts/sync-skills.ts` generates each skill into `~/.pi/agent/skills/` (Pi), `~/.codex/skills/` (Codex), and `~/.claude/skills/` (Claude Code). Generated directories carry a `.managed-by-pi-skills` marker and are replaced on every sync. Never write a skill into them, into `~/.agents/skills/`, or into a project's `.claude/skills/`.
+
+**Sync:** run `bun ~/.pi/scripts/sync-skills.ts` after every change. It exits non-zero when a skill fails and keeps that skill's previous output. `~/.pi/scripts/install.nu` also runs it.
+
+**Frontmatter consumed by the sync** (the header of `sync-skills.ts` is the full reference):
+- `targets: [pi, codex, claude]` limits which harnesses receive the skill. Default: all.
+- `source:` adopts an upstream skill (`git` with optional `path` and `ref`, or `command`) instead of copying it. Local frontmatter keys override upstream keys, a local SKILL.md body is appended to the upstream body, and local files overlay upstream files.
+- `disable-model-invocation: true` makes the skill manual-only on every harness.
+
+Each harness receives only the frontmatter keys it supports; the sync filters the rest.
+
+**Changing a sourced skill:** copy the upstream skill directory at the pinned `ref` into a scratch git repo and commit it. Edit, then save `git diff` as `~/.pi/skills/<name>/upstream.patch`. Re-run the sync to confirm the patch applies.
+
+**Runtime paths:** each harness installs the skill at a different path, and the agent's working directory is not the skill directory. For any file the agent runs or reads from a shell, write `{{skillDir}}/scripts/tool.sh` in a local file. The sync expands `{{skillDir}}` per harness, but only in local files, not upstream ones.
 
